 Lou Hamer), and by children, featuring the unique ways children express and understand themselves and the world through song. And each is made with listeners of all ages in mind! Since its founding in 1948, Folkways has placed music by and for children  at the heart of its mission to document “the people’s music.” Bringing together new and traditional children’s folk music classics and music from diverse cultures, our “Growing Up” card pack encourages children to learn through interactive movement and develop their senses of self and community through song.","seriestitle":"Growing Up with Smithsonian Folkways","accents":[],"authors":[],"narrators":[],"copyrights":["©"],"cover":{"imageL":"https://card-content.yotoplay.com/yoto/pub/uEdZwNW_Uxwx6jZRu0g1VkI9hehtHgtDZ_8tIf1CQKg"},"languages":["en"],"media":{"duration":2269,"fileSize":36696114,"hasStreams":false},"status":{"name":"complete","updatedAt":"2026-05-12T09:50:19.636Z"}},"cardId":"crjfS","createdAt":"2025-01-28T16:24:58.332Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-12T09:50:04.075Z"},"ownership":{"canAccess":true,"userHasRole":false,"cardIsFree":false,"cardIsMadeByUser":false,"cardIsInFamilyLibrary":false,"cardIsCreatedByFamily":false,"isAccessibleUsingSubscription":false,"isAccessibleAsPhysicalPlay":false,"isShareLink":false,"isReconditionCard":false,"inCardPacks":false,"previewAccessOnly":true}}